From: crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not build the test programs

Celluloid has no meson option to switch its test programs off: meson.build
enters the "test" subdirectory unconditionally, so test-option-parser and
test-playlist-model are compiled on every build (they are not installed, but
they are still built and run by "meson test"). This repository does not build
tests at all, see the repository rules, so the subdirectory is dropped.
---
 meson.build | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -60,6 +60,5 @@
 subdir('data')
 subdir('docs')
 subdir('po')
-subdir('test')
 
 meson.add_install_script('meson-post-install.py')
